            <ArticleTitle>Headache attributed to unruptured saccular aneurysm, mimicking hemicrania continua.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>156-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Unruptured cerebral arterial aneurysms most often remain asymptomatic, but they may cause headache or other symptoms or signs. We describe herewith a case of headache attributed to an unruptured internal carotid artery aneurysm, clearly mimicking the phenotype of hemicrania continua. Potential pathophysiological explanations and recommendations for recognition of similar cases are discussed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
